<!-- formalization -->

**Definition (`InfoSys.idMap`).** The identity approximable mapping on an information system relates consistent sets $u$ and $v$ precisely when $u$ entails $v$.

**Theorem (`InfoSys.idMap.toElement`).** The element map of the identity approximable mapping is the identity on elements.

*Proof.* Relatedness yields entailment of singletons, so tokens of the image lie in the source element by closure; conversely each token is recovered from its singleton via reflexivity of entailment. □
